error[Z0401]: `fe:` takes fixed effects joined by `+`, and `firm * year` uses `*`, which it does not admit
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: firm * year)
  |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^ not a fixed effect
  |
  = help: `fe:` admits `+` and `:` only: write `fe: a + b` for two effects, or `fe: a:b` for their interaction
----
error[Z0401]: `fe:` takes fixed effects joined by `+`, and `educ..exper` is a range of variables
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: educ..exper)
  |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^ not a fixed effect
  |
  = help: name each effect: `fe: firm + year`
----
error[Z0401]: `fe:` takes fixed effects joined by `+`, and `log(firm)` is an expression, not a variable
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: log(firm))
  |                             ^^^^^^^^^ not a fixed effect
  |
  = help: a fixed effect is a variable of the frame, or an interaction `a:b` of two; compute a new variable with `add` first
----
error[Z0401]: `fe:` takes fixed effects joined by `+`, and `1` is not one: the intercept is absorbed by the effects
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: firm - 1)
  |                             ^^^^^^^^ not a fixed effect
  |
  = help: write the effects alone, `fe: firm + year`
----
error[Z0401]: `fe:` takes fixed effects joined by `+`, and `1` is not one: the intercept is absorbed by the effects
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: 1)
  |                             ^ not a fixed effect
  |
  = help: write the effects alone, `fe: firm + year`
----
error[Z0401]: `firm` is a fixed effect of `fe:` and a variable of the formula too
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:36
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + firm, fe: firm)
  |                                    ^^^^ absorbed and in the model
  |
  = help: an absorbed effect cannot be a regressor or the outcome as well; drop it from `fe:` or from the formula
----
error[Z0410]: `se: hc3` and `fe:` exclude each other: with absorbed effects an observation's leverage in the full design is not available
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:44
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: firm:year, se: hc3)
  |                                            ^^^ needs every observation's leverage
  |
  = help: `se: robust` (HC1) or `cluster:` with `fe:`; HC2 and HC3 with fixed effects arrive with release 0.8.0
----
error[Z0304]: `influence` on a fit with fixed effects is not available in this release
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: firm).influence()
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a fit with `fe:`
  |
  = help: the leverage, Cook's distance and studentized residuals of a fit with absorbed effects arrive with release 0.8.0; `residuals()` and `fitted()` are available now
----
error[Z0101]: no variable `nowhere` in `w`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ, fe: nowhere)
  |                             ^^^^^^^ not a variable of w
  |
  = help: the variables of `w` are: worker, year, wage, educ, exper, age, hours, union and 3 more
